nodes.bodyText:
Motivation
Currently Object Oriented libraries that permit stateful operations, such Linen and NNX, perform context-dependent checks when an object is being updated to avoid tracer leakage. However, both Linen and NNX use the current top trace as a proxy of the current transform they are in:
def current_trace():
  return jax.core.find_top_trace(())

This mechanism is very unreliable as the top trace doesn't get updated in transform's such as jax.vmap.
Proposal
Improve safety for library code, here we propose the TransformContext API. The sole purpose of this API is to signal whether or not the current transform context is the same as the context in which a TransformContext object was created.
class TransformContext(Hashable):
  def is_current(self) -> bool: ...
The .is_current() would return True if its being called inside the same transform it was created or false otherwise.
Expected behavior
Trivial eager
tc = TransformContext()
assert tc.is_current()
Trivial jit
@jax.jit
def f():
  tc = TransformContext()
  assert tc.is_current()
f()
Captured jit
tc = TransformContext()

@jax.jit
def f():
  assert not tc.is_current()
f()
Escaped jit
tc = None

@jax.jit
def f():
  global tc
  tc = TransformContext()

f()
assert not tc.is_current()
Escaped + captured at same level
tc = None

@jax.jit
def f():
  global tc
  tc = TransformContext()

f()

@jax.jit
def g():
  assert not tc.is_current()
g()
Nested jit-jit
@jax.jit
def f():
  tc = TransformContext()

  @jax.jit
  def g():
    assert not tc.is_current()
  g()
f()
Nested jit-vmap
@jax.jit
def f():
  tc = TransformContext()

  @jax.vmap
  def g(_i):
    assert not tc.is_current()
  g(jnp.array([1,2,3]))
f()
